PS-API-5  graphCheck accepts duplicate vertex labels
  gcc -I<build>/include tl.c -L<build>/lib -lscotch -lscotcherr -lz -lpthread -lm -o tl
  LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<build>/lib ./tl 0   (unique labels)  -> graphCheck=0
  LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<build>/lib ./tl 1   (vlbltab {0,0,1,2})
PRISTINE: ./tl 1 -> graphCheck=0 (duplicate accepted).
PATCHED : ./tl 1 -> "graphCheck: duplicate vertex label", graphCheck=1. ./tl 0 still 0.
Note: the parttab printed by tl (5 -1 -1 -1) is identical for ./tl 0 and ./tl 1 and for
pristine and patched, so this kit does NOT demonstrate any wrong part assignment by
graphTabLoad; only the graphCheck result differs. The consumer-side effect of duplicate
labels is not demonstrated here.
